  "labelNotes": "Supply range from Recommended Operating Conditions (VIN 2.7-5.5 V). ISHDN/IQ rows print 'IOUT = 0' with no unit, so that condition is left out (VIN = +5V is a table-wide header default, also left out). ILEAK 'Input Leakage Current' (Disabled, OUT grounded, 1 uA max) is the power switch's IN-to-OUT off-state leakage on the power input, not a digital/control pin and not a supply current of the part; deliberately excluded from both fields (doubtful). IREV reverse leakage excluded. ISINK 'EN Input Leakage' (VEN = 5V, not an allowed key) labelled. Abs max: VIN 6.5 V and VEN/VFLG 6.5 V give the same (value, unit, qualifier) so one label; VOUT 'VIN +0.3' skipped as an expression. 'Input Voltage' also occurs in the ROC VIN line and the VIH/VIL EN lines on page 3."
